{
  "version": "1.4",
  "description": "V13.12b ORDERED-ORIENTATION STRUCTURAL CAPACITY STRESS-TEST SPACE — diagnostic only. Updated by V13.21 for unconstrained MSM relative diagnosis multipliers. Do NOT use as a production calibration space. Same widened stress-test space as V13.12, but fixes Female orientation contact multiplier to 1.0, samples Heterosexual_Male above that reference, and samples MSM at or above Heterosexual_Male. This removes the invalid orientation proposals seen in V13.12 while testing whether a higher heterosexual male contact multiplier materially shifts capacity.",
  "notes": [
    "STRESS-TEST ONLY. Do not run an ABC-SMC production calibration from this space.",
    "Ordered-orientation diagnostic: Female = 1.0, Heterosexual_Male sampled from 1.0 to 3.0, MSM sampled from Heterosexual_Male to 7.0.",
    "This is not a literature-backed production assumption; it is a side run to test whether ordered higher heterosexual/MSM orientation multipliers materially shift capacity.",
    "activity_low (derived) can reach ~0.84 at extremes; runner mask enforces activity_low in [0.14, 0.81].",
    "Wide diagnosis / ART / contact bounds exist to test model structural capacity, not as priors.",
    "msm_relative_diagnosis_enabled fixed True activates the MSM relative diagnosis multiplier for all particles."
  ],
